From fbd8509ea1e87a7fadb7b75dfc7373fc27469342 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 13:56:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fixup! logging: write log lines on a logger thread

Stop, join and drain the consumer before fork; restart it independently in parent and child, also on parent-side fork failure. Preserve fork errno. The daemon and LockDirectory native fixture use the explicit operation. Application producers/configuration must be quiescent, with no live event builder and child-compatible sinks/callbacks; no arbitrary concurrent-fork safety claim, producer hot-path overhead or disabled child logger.

Original focused LockDirectory test hangs before correction (bounded8s timeout), then passes. Bounded repeated-fork native regression checks child WARN/ERROR delivery and flush, continued parent delivery and exactly-once queued parent marker. Original-owner test deliberately avoids later typed-event and FinishLogging APIs. All five actual source targets and both focused native regressions plus complete logging native suites pass. Full standard post-correction gate is separate and not claimed here.

Artifact real logger controls cover child typed Error/FinishLogging,131072 full-ring backlog records actually written plus full-ring WARN/ERROR,zero drops, pre-start buffering/no thread, injected EAGAIN/errno preservation and parent restart. Correctness counts, not throughput. Independent original-prefix syntax review and context transport are recorded separately. Manually authored lifecycle fix, not a scripted call conversion.
